# Line endings are LF, in the repository AND in the working tree.
#
# `eol=lf` IS LOAD-BEARING AND IS NOT THE DEFAULT. `text=auto` on its own
# stores LF in the object database but converts on CHECKOUT to `core.eol`,
# which defaults to `native` - CRLF on Windows. `core.autocrlf=false` does NOT
# prevent that: autocrlf is the legacy fallback and is ignored once a path has
# an explicit `text` attribute. So the checkout side is pinned rather than left
# to the platform.
#
# This was not theoretical here. The first clone taken to extract this
# repository checked out CRLF, because .gitattributes had not been committed
# yet, and a scripted edit matching a two-line pattern silently found nothing.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Test vectors: timing arrays with seed-regenerated material. Small and
# tracked on purpose so the replay tests travel with the package - but never
# converted, and never diffed as text.
*.npz binary
*.npy binary
*.bin binary
*.elf binary
